#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""owi-serve — the local graphical OWI Office.

    tools/owi-serve                 # open the real local workspace
    tools/owi-serve --home PATH     # use an existing OWI workspace
    tools/owi-serve --demo          # explicitly create/use sample data

The default start never invents or silently installs a workforce. If the
selected workspace has no public index, the graphical office opens in a clear
setup state with no model, ability, or price rows. ``--demo`` is the only
server path that seeds the repository's sample roster.

With a configured workspace, picks are derived from its stored snapshot and
private ledger. Execution uses YOUR command from runners.json (your CLI, your
key — the server never holds credentials), and your worked/didn't answer is
recorded to the private ledger.

Binds to 127.0.0.1 by default. The page can only name a model; the command that
runs is resolved server-side from runners.json, and the task text travels on
stdin — nothing from the browser is ever executed as shell.
"""

